@startuml
' The opening (core): language, problem and order number, before the problem's flow starts
!include _style.iuml
hide empty description
skinparam state {
  BorderColor $STEP_LINE
  BackgroundColor $STEP_BG
  AttributeFontSize 11
  AttributeFontColor $MUTED
  BackgroundColor<<ask>> $ASK_BG
  BorderColor<<ask>> $ASK_LINE
  BackgroundColor<<llm>> $LLM_BG
  BorderColor<<llm>> $LLM_LINE
}
hide stereotype

state "Analyze the first message" as FIRST <<llm>> : <i>one call: the language and the issue</i>\n<i>the number: regular expression</i>
state CANDIDATES <<choice>>
state "Confirm the issue" as CONFIRM <<ask>> : <i>choice: the candidates + <U+201C>something else<U+201D></i>
state "Describe the issue" as DESCRIBE <<ask>> : <i>free text, then one call: the issue</i>\n<i>the number, if present</i>
state NUMBER_KNOWN <<choice>>
state "Ask for the order number" as NUMBER <<ask>> : <i>text, read by regular expression</i>
state "The issue's flow" as FLOW : <i>CANCEL, DAMAGED…</i>

[*] --> FIRST : first message
FIRST --> CANDIDATES
DESCRIBE --> CANDIDATES
CANDIDATES --> CONFIRM : confidence ≥ 0.7: the most likely alone\notherwise: all those with probability > 0
CANDIDATES --> DESCRIBE : no candidate\n(<U+201C>other<U+201D>)
CONFIRM --> DESCRIBE : <U+201C>something else<U+201D>
CONFIRM --> NUMBER_KNOWN : issue chosen
NUMBER_KNOWN --> FLOW : number known
NUMBER_KNOWN --> NUMBER : number missing
NUMBER -[dashed]-> NUMBER : <size:10>ORDER_NUMBER_UNREADABLE</size>
NUMBER --> FLOW : number read
FLOW --> [*]

note right of CONFIRM
  Even when confident, the model never decides alone:
  the customer always confirms their issue.
  Uncertainty only changes the number of choices offered.
end note
note bottom of DESCRIBE
  No way out other than choosing an issue:
  there is no human handover yet.
end note
@enduml
